        "subject": "LU-20354 quota: complete per-stype qmt_sarr API",
        "message": "LU-20354 quota: complete per-stype qmt_sarr API\n\nde71b51fad split pool membership into tgts[QMT_STYPE_CNT], but\nthe qmt_sarr_* helpers (lock, get_idx, count, rem, check_idx)\nstill cover only the primary array, so qmt_sum_lqe_usg() takes\nqpi_sarr()->op_rw_sem and walks op_array directly, and the MD\nusage cache would have to do the same.\n\nAdd per-stype lock macros, qmt_sarr_get_idx_stype() and\nqmt_sarr_count_stype(), and build the primary helpers on them.\nqmt_sarr_pool_rem() and qmt_sarr_check_idx() take a stype.  Add\nqmt_sarr_for_each() to call a callback for each member of every\ninitialized array under that array's op_rw_sem, and use it in\nqmt_sum_lqe_usg() so the sarr internals stay in qmt_pool.c.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-quota\nSigned-off-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Cursor:Composer\nChange-Id: I742742133ffc818e88e3ed31f1377ed083ac6c44\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
